{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Spline Handle Choice for Rotoscopy.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Spline Handle Choice for Rotoscopy.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"spline handle choice for rotoscopy spline handle choice for rotoscopy","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Spline Handle Choice for Rotoscopy.md","fileName":"Spline Handle Choice for Rotoscopy.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Spline Handle Choice for Rotoscopy","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-15 18:17\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Rotoscopy and Motion Tracking]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Rotoscopy and Motion Tracking","Segmenting Moving Roto Shapes","digitalvisualeffectsandcompositing.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Spline Handle Choice for Rotoscopy.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Spline Handle Choice for Rotoscopy.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"spline handle choice for rotoscopy spline handle choice for rotoscopy","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Spline Handle Choice for Rotoscopy.md","fileName":"Spline Handle Choice for Rotoscopy.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Spline Handle Choice for Rotoscopy","heading":"Spline Handle Choice for Rotoscopy","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Spline type affects how a roto contour bends between control points. A Bezier spline can hold a sharp change of direction through its handles, while a B-spline tends to produce a smoother curve with tension distributed across neighboring points. A smooth contour with unnecessarily many points becomes difficult to animate and may wobble. The best choice follows the subject's actual silhouette rather than a habit of adding vertices. See [[Segmenting Moving Roto Shapes]] for why separate shapes also reduce contour complexity.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Rotoscopy and Motion Tracking","Segmenting Moving Roto Shapes","digitalvisualeffectsandcompositing.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Spline Handle Choice for Rotoscopy.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Spline Handle Choice for Rotoscopy.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"spline handle choice for rotoscopy spline handle choice for rotoscopy","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Spline Handle Choice for Rotoscopy.md","fileName":"Spline Handle Choice for Rotoscopy.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Spline Handle Choice for Rotoscopy","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[digitalvisualeffectsandcompositing.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Rotoscopy and Motion Tracking","Segmenting Moving Roto Shapes","digitalvisualeffectsandcompositing.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}